OLLOWS_RATIO for outlier detection.\n# Usefulness: Adjusts scale while accounting for extreme values.\n\n# CIRCULARITY_COMPACTNESS\n# Ratio of DISTANCE_CIRCULARITY to SQRT_COMPACTNESS, quantifying compactness relative to circular characteristics.\n# Usefulness: Differentiates compact, circular shapes typical of certain silhouettes.\n\n# ELONG_SCATTER_RATIO\n# Ratio of ELONGATEDNESS to SCATTER_RATIO.\n# Usefulness: Highlights joint contributions of elongation and scatter for key silhouette differentiations.\n\n# ELONG_SCATTER_INTERACTION\n# Multiplication of ELONGATEDNESS and SCATTER_RATIO.\n# Usefulness: Creates a higher-order interaction term amplifying elongated, scattered effects typical of categories like BUS or VAN.\n\n# LOG_SCALED_VARIANCE_MINOR\n# Log-transform of SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS to reduce skew.\n# Usefulness: Lowers variance impacts while emphasizing smaller but critical differences across samples.\n\n# ZSCALED_RADIUS_DIFF\n# Z-score normalization of SCALED_RADIUS_MIN_VAR_DIFF.\n# Usefulness: Removes magnitude bias in derived radius-variance differences, useful across all silhouette types.\n\n# NORMALIZED_RADIUS_RATIO\n# Min-max normalization of RADIUS_RATIO to scale radius ranges between 0-1.\n# Usefulness: Highlights relative radius variations proportionally.\n\n# HOLLOWS_RATIO_RESCALED\n# Reciprocal of HOLLOWS_RATIO emphasizing smaller values.\n# Usefulness: Amplifies the impact of lower hollow-area-to-polygon ratios.", "df.drop(columns=[\n    'SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS', \n    'RADIUS_RATIO', \n    'DISTANCE_CIRCULARITY'\n], inplace=True)"]
